  "notes": "The priest's own confession, said bowed at the foot of the altar before the ministers repeat it. The corpus already carries the ministers' branch as ordinarium.confiteor (variant ministrorum); this is its counterpart, and the two differ in exactly two places: vobis, fratres at w022-w023 and vos, fratres at w058-w059, where the ministers say tibi, pater and te, pater. Witness do prints the priest's text in full and gives the ministers' as a substitution rule (et ubi a Sacerdote dicebatur vobis, fratres, et vos, fratres, a Ministris dicitur tibi, pater, et te, pater), which is why every other word is shared. The answer to this confession is ordinarium.misereatur-tui, not ordinarium.misereatur: the ministers say Misereátur tui back to the priest, and the priest says Misereátur vestri over them after their own confession. FRATRES at w023 and w059 is tagged vocative although the plural of frater is identical in the nominative, the accusative and the vocative; the case rests on the address, exactly as pater does in the ministers' branch. Rubric s04 is DO's inline '(Percutit sibi pectus ter, dicens:)' as its own segment, here in the singular the missal prints for the priest.",
